#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""herdr-crew: gives each coding agent in Herdr its crew personality.

  herdr-crew session-start    Claude Code SessionStart hook: picks this terminal's robot (or keeps
                              the one it has), labels the terminal herdr.crew=<id> so Herdr's Crew
                              panel shows the same robot, and prints the persona as extra context.
  herdr-crew persona [id]     the persona text (this terminal's robot when no id is given), for
                              agents without hooks (Codex reads it via its instructions file)
  herdr-crew whoami           this terminal's robot id
  herdr-crew roster [--json]  every running agent: robot name, provider, address, machine, space,
                              status, and which one is you (also given to Claude at session start)
  herdr-crew wait <for> [note] [--for 30m]
                              mark this agent as waiting (shown in Herdr until its next turn starts):
                              <for> is ci, pr, tests, deploy, agent, you, timer or other
  herdr-crew wait --clear     not waiting any more
  (touch ~/.herdr/crew-no-persona to keep the roster but drop the persona text at session start)

Outside a Herdr terminal (no HC_TERMINAL_ID) it does nothing. Personas are condensed and
paraphrased from MIT-licensed role prompts: wshobson/agents, lst97/claude-code-sub-agents,
iannuttall/claude-agents, VoltAgent/awesome-claude-code-subagents.
"""
